#DESCRIPTION
2-level AMR force-free current sheet, hybrid PIC: coarse-fine interface quality

The force-free sheet of ../reconnection/PARAM.in.forcefree_hybrid (Le et al.
2016; lambda = 1 d_i, Bg = 0.3 B0, beta_i = 0.5, Ti/Te = 5, uniform density)
on a 10 x 5 d_i box: base 32 x 16 (dx = 0.3125 d_i, the resolution of the
uniform deck) with a 2x refined patch around the X-point, for half an ion
gyroperiod. In this equilibrium |B| = sqrt(B0^2 + Bg^2) and n are uniform, so
any structure the coarse-fine interface imprints on the field stands out.
validate.py checks the interface diagnostics (divB-AMR: div(B) at the
interface, drift of the first fine ghost layer) and the uniformity of |B|^2 on
both levels at the start and at the end.

